# Casino Syndicate

Vite/React/Redux UI (`app`), Hardhat contracts (`contracts`). `GameFactory` creates games by `GameType`; roulette is one type. Redux via `app/core/store.js`.

## Style

- No semicolons, no trailing commas, double quotes, 2-space indent, max 160 cols
- Prefer lodash (`import _ from "lodash"`) at call site over one-off helpers or native equivalents
- No one-off named helpers/wrappers — extract only when reused 2+ times
- Destructure with `|| {}` / `|| []`; avoid `?.` for field reads (optional calls OK)
- No nested ternaries; name booleans. JSX: `&&` not ternary. Imperative: `if`, not `&&`
- No defensive code: no try/catch unless recovering; no fallbacks for required data/env
- Rem for custom sizes (often `0.75rem`). Minimal diffs

## UI (`app`)

- Imports from `app/`: `core/`, `screens/`, `components/`, `games/`
- `actions`/`store` from `app/core/store.js`
- `React.useState` etc. — never destructure built-ins from `"react"` (third-party hooks unprefixed)
- Redux only: `actions.get/set/update/unset`; `useSelector(() => selectX())`; fetch then select
- Domain modules: selectors → fetchers → mutators → mappers. Fetchers write store only (no side effects)
- Loaders: `setLoader`/`clearLoader`. No nested components, no single-use hooks/JSX vars — Redux + core/games instead
- Mantine + SCSS (not Tailwind). Persist via `PERSISTENT_PATHS` — never localforage from domain modules
- Material Design, minimal: quiet gray surfaces, clear hierarchy, one primary action per screen
- Chrome (header, page, modal header) uses `gray.1` / `gray.2` — not white-on-white, not casino felt/brass/gold
- Mantine components over custom chrome; FABs for screen actions; no extra frames, docks, or ornamental UI
- Mantine `NumberInput` for numeric values (amounts, min, max) — not `TextInput`. Keep stepper controls; do not `hideControls`. Clamp on submit, not on each keystroke

## Contracts

- Game logic lives on the game contract (`Roulette.sol`). Factory only creates, indexes, and stores `GameType`
- Solidity keeps required semicolons; do not apply the JS style rules to `.sol`
